@page "/marten"
@using MartenStudio.Services.Settings
@inject StudioDescriptor Descriptor

@*
    The studio's root page. One route, one endpoint, whatever studio is mapped: the body is the descriptor's
    OverviewComponent - MartenStudio's store overview, another studio's own - and this page names no studio's
    component itself (design PS5, §2.5).

    A body slot rather than two routed components, because two components claiming the root would be two
    endpoints on one pattern: an AmbiguousMatchException at request time, and a relative route the route table
    refuses. The body keeps everything a page has - its <PageTitle>, its [SupplyParameterFromQuery] properties,
    its scope subscription - because nothing about any of those depends on being the routed component.

    The compile-time root is this assembly's (StudioPageAssembly); the endpoint mapping re-roots it under the
    configured mount path like every other page.
*@

<DynamicComponent Type="@Descriptor.OverviewComponent" />
